/*
 * Preflight - the baseline every utility outranks.
 *
 * Tailwind v4's preflight zeroes margin and padding on every element, and CSS starts every element at
 * white-space: normal and flex-shrink: 1. Velvet gives the Labels it creates (VNodePool.VelvetLabelClassName)
 * those values; a Label UI Toolkit builds inside its own control keeps the theme's. The rule is imported
 * ahead of every utility sheet, so a `p-*`, `m-*`, `whitespace-*` or `shrink-*` on the same element ties
 * with it on specificity and wins on order.
 *
 * The generator's utility table does not read this sheet (StyleUtilityTableBuilder.PreflightSheetName).
 */

.velvet-label { margin: 0; padding: 0; white-space: normal; flex-shrink: 1; }
